                    <occupation>Lawyer and politician</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Perhaps Philip Champion de Crespigny Hist of Parl d.1803 noted as a man
                            of fashion and about 70 years old by 1800. His brother Sir Claude
                            Champion de Crespigny born 1734 will PCC 1818 had "the honour of
                            receiving the Prince Regent" (Burke's Peerage de Crespigny) at his
                            Camberwell home (and so perhaps the most likely companion of the
                            Prince's ex-mistress Mary Robinson) made a baronet 1805. He married Mary
                            Clarke 1764. Their sons Claude d.1813, Sir William will PCC 1830,
                            Augustin will PCC 1826, all in Royal Navy, Heaton d 1858, Herbert Joseph
                        </p>
